    "notes": [
      "Phase 3 is still non-removal: BrowserActivity, BrowserScreen, AppRoute.Browser, WebView, browser launchers, browser persistence, and manifest browser filters remain present.",
      "Classifies reviewed handoffs as direct file, direct media, adaptive HLS/DASH, torrent, or page/unknown without starting a transfer.",
      "Preserves normalized MIME type, positive content length, page URL/title context, and a safe source label through AutomationCommandDraft and DownloadIntakeDraft.",
      "Adds an explicit Inspect as media action that creates or updates the existing media-workbench record and navigates to Media without starting yt-dlp, a worker, a backend, or a queue item.",
      "Preserves external share, VIEW, download-manager and Tasker intake, native and aria2 engines, scheduler, workers, Termux/yt-dlp, media resolution, offline library, playback, Room schema 14, versionCode 21, and versionName 0.20.0-rc08.",
      "Historical browser-era validators now recognize the ordered browser-removal overlay family while retaining their runtime and architecture assertions.",
      "All 59 validators invoked by the current final static gate pass, shell and Python syntax checks pass, and the focused JVM harness passes 16 assertions.",
      "Full Gradle validation could not run in this sandbox because Gradle 9.4.1 is not cached and network access is disabled; Devtool validation remains required in the target Android environment."
    ]
